{"unit_id": "script_0001", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 1}, "text": "# Lecture 7: parallelism", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0002", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 2}, "text": "Last week: parallelism within a single GPU", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0003", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 3}, "text": "This week: parallelism across multiple GPUs", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0004", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 4}, "text": "In both cases, **compute** (arithmetic logic units) is far from inputs/outputs (**data**).", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0005", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 5}, "text": "Unifying theme: orchestrate computation to avoid data transfer bottlenecks", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0006", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 6}, "text": "Generalized hierarchy:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0007", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 7}, "text": "- Single node, single GPU: L1 cache / shared memory (fastest)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0008", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 8}, "text": "- Single node, single GPU: HBM", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0009", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 9}, "text": "- Single node, multi-GPU: NVLink/NVSwitch", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0010", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 10}, "text": "- Multi-node, multi-GPU: Infiniband/Ethernet (slowest)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0011", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 11}, "text": "Last week: reduce memory accesses via fusion/tiling", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0012", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 12}, "text": "This week: reduce communication across GPUs/nodes via replication/sharding", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0013", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 13}, "text": "Why do multi-GPU?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0014", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 14}, "text": "1. Your parameters (optimizer state + gradients + activations) don't fit on a single GPU.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0015", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 15}, "text": "2. You want to use more GPUs (more FLOPs) to train faster.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0016", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 16}, "text": "### Part 1: building blocks of distributed communication/computation", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0017", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 17}, "text": "### Part 2: distributed training", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0018", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 18}, "text": "Walk through bare-bones implementations of each strategy on deep MLPs.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0019", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 19}, "text": "Recall that MLPs are the compute bottleneck in Transformers, so this is representative.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0020", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 20}, "text": "What's missing?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0021", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 21}, "text": "- Communication/computation overlap", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0022", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 22}, "text": "- More general models (with attention, etc.)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0023", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 23}, "text": "- Other forms of parallelism (e.g., sequence parallelism, expert parallelism, combinations)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0024", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 24}, "text": "- But we're doing PyTorch so you can see how one builds up from the primitives", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0025", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 25}, "text": "### Summary", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0026", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 26}, "text": "- Many ways to parallelize: data (batch), tensor/expert (width), pipeline (depth), sequence (length)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0027", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 27}, "text": "- Data parallelism: DDP (all-reduce), FSDP/ZeRO (all-gather + reduce-scatter)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0028", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 28}, "text": "- Tensor parallelism: requires very fast interconnects (e.g., NVLink)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0029", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 29}, "text": "- Pipeline parallelism: can work with slow interconnects, but need to work to reduce pipeline bubbles", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0030", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 30}, "text": "- Can **re-compute** or store in **memory** or store in another GPUs memory and **communicate**", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0031", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 31}, "text": "- Hardware is getting faster, but will always want bigger models, so will have this hierarchical structure", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0032", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 32}, "text": "- These are classic in the parallel programming literature from the 1980s.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0033", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 33}, "text": "- *Collective* means that you specify a general communication pattern across many devices.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0034", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 34}, "text": "- This can be better/faster than managing point-to-point communication yourself.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0035", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 35}, "text": "**Setup**:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0036", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 36}, "text": "- **Rank**: a particular device/GPU (e.g., 0, 1, 2, 3)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0037", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 37}, "text": "- **World size**: total number of devices (e.g., 4)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0038", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 38}, "text": "Operations:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0039", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 39}, "text": "- Broadcast, scatter, gather, reduce (foundations)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0040", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 40}, "text": "- All-gather, reduce-scatter, all-reduce (workhorse)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0041", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 41}, "text": "- All-to-all (for MoEs)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0042", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 42}, "text": "**Broadcast**: copy from rank 0 to all ranks", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0043", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 43}, "text": "Minor use case: rank 0 loads initial checkpoint and broadcasts to all ranks", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0044", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 44}, "text": "**Scatter** tensor on rank 0 to all ranks", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0045", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 45}, "text": "Note: stepping stone to understanding reduce-scatter", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0046", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 46}, "text": "**Gather** pieces from all ranks to rank 0 (opposite of scatter)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0047", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 47}, "text": "Note: stepping stone to understanding all-gather", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0048", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 48}, "text": "**Reduce** pieces from all ranks to rank 0, applying some operation (e.g., sum, min, max)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0049", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 49}, "text": "Note: stepping stone to understanding all-reduce", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0050", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 50}, "text": "**All-gather**: perform gather to all ranks, not just rank 0", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0051", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 51}, "text": "Use case: each rank holds parameter shard, gather to get full parameters for forward pass", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0052", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 52}, "text": "**Reduce-scatter**: perform reduce on each dimension, scatter results", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0053", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 53}, "text": "Use case: after backward pass, sum gradients from different data shards, but distribute storage", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0054", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 54}, "text": "**All-reduce** = reduce-scatter + all-gather", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0055", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 55}, "text": "Use case: after backward pass, sum gradients from different data shards, but replicate full parameters", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0056", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 56}, "text": "Breaking all-reduce into reduce-scatter + all-gather allows for flexibility (e.g., ZeRO/FSDP)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0057", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 57}, "text": "**All-to-all**: each rank sends each other rank some tensor (most general)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0058", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 58}, "text": "Notes:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0059", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 59}, "text": "- Useful for MoEs: each rank has split of data and subset of experts; need to route data to experts", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0060", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 60}, "text": "- For balanced splits, all-to-all looks like transpose", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0061", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 61}, "text": "- Also handles unbalanced splits (but want splits to be as balanced as possible)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0062", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 62}, "text": "Way to remember the terminology:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0063", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 63}, "text": "- Reduce: performs some associative/commutative operation (sum, min, max)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0064", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 64}, "text": "- Scatter is inverse of gather", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0065", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 65}, "text": "- All: means destination is all devices", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0066", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 66}, "text": "Classic (in the home):", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0067", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 67}, "text": "- GPUs on different nodes communicate via Ethernet (~200 MB/s)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0068", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 68}, "text": "Modern (in the data center):", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0069", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 69}, "text": "Typical setup:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0070", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 70}, "text": "- 8 GPUs per node, connected by NVLink to an NVSwitch (B200s' NVLink 5.0 gets 1.8 TB/s; HBM was 8 TB/s)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0071", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 71}, "text": "- 256 nodes per pod, connected by Infiniband (via PCIe -> HCA / Infiniband NIC -> Infiniband cable) (~0.05 TB/s)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0072", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 72}, "text": "- N pods per cluster / datacenter, connected by Ethernet (via PCIe -> CPU)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0073", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 73}, "text": "Bypassing the CPU:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0074", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 74}, "text": "- Ethernet requires passing through the CPU (copying data to kernel socket buffer, build TCP packets, copy to NIC ring buffer)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0075", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 75}, "text": "- Remote Direct Memory Access (RDMA): allows one GPU to directly read/write another GPU's memory without involving the CPU", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0076", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 76}, "text": "- Infiniband supports RDMA, but standard Ethernet does not", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0077", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 77}, "text": "Advancements:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0078", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 78}, "text": "- GB200/GB300 NVL72: 8 GPUs per tray, 9 trays per rack -> 72 GPUs in one NVLink domain", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0079", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 79}, "text": "- RDMA over Converged Ethernet (RoCE): Ethernet bypasses CPU, similar but cheaper/weaker than Infiniband, used by Meta", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0080", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 80}, "text": "### NVIDIA Collective Communication Library (NCCL)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0081", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 81}, "text": "- Detects topology of hardware (e.g., number of nodes, switches, NVLink/PCIe)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0082", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 82}, "text": "- Optimizes the path between GPUs", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0083", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 83}, "text": "- Launches GPU kernels to send/receive data", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0084", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 84}, "text": "- Provides clean interface for collective operations (e.g., `all_gather_into_tensor`)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0085", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 85}, "text": "- Supports multiple backends for different hardware: gloo (CPU), nccl (GPU)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0086", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 86}, "text": "- Also supports higher-level algorithms (e.g., `FullyShardedDataParallel`) [not used in this course]", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0087", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 87}, "text": "Let's walk through some examples.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0088", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 88}, "text": "Indeed, all-reduce = reduce-scatter + all-gather!", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0089", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 89}, "text": "How fast does communication happen?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0090", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 90}, "text": "References:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0091", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 91}, "text": "Sharding strategy: each rank gets a slice of the data", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0092", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 92}, "text": "Notes:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0093", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 93}, "text": "- Losses are different across ranks (computed on local data)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0094", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 94}, "text": "- Gradients are all-reduced to be the same across ranks", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0095", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 95}, "text": "- Therefore, parameters remain the same across ranks", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0096", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 96}, "text": "Next time: FSDP/ZeRO: use all-gather and reduce-scatter to avoid holding all parameters in memory", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0097", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 97}, "text": "Sharding strategy: each rank gets part of each layer, transfer all data/activations", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0098", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 98}, "text": "Sharding strategy: each rank gets subset of layers, transfer all data/activations", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0099", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 99}, "text": "Not handled: overlapping communication/computation to eliminate pipeline bubbles", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0100", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 100}, "text": "- Jax/TPUs: just define the model, the sharding strategy, and the Jax compiler handles the rest", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0101", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_07.py", "loc": {"block": 101}, "text": "**Collective operations** are the conceptual primitives used for distributed programming", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
